# Buffer.alloc(1); JSON.parse(text).from("hi")
# `from` is called on a value that nobody knows, and objects of the class Buffer exist. But nobody has come by `Buffer` itself out of sight: it is named, and a member of it is called, in sight.
# So `from` is not looked for on it, and the function of the library behind Buffer.from is not in the program.
# The other half: property-found-off-a-value-that-nobody-knows-hands-out-the-built-in-that-its-row-answers.ir.
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK: function f1 unreached

